// ability key or Type Tag as a resist/weakness match — every real usage today is a plain damage
// type (heat:7, poison:6, cold:4, acid:3; weakness usage is entirely empty) — so trimming this
// list can't break existing card data. The rule applied: keep an ability key only if it
// describes an inherent, permanent quality of HOW THIS CARD DEALS DAMAGE (a sensible thing to
// resist/be weak to — Pierce, Crit, Siege, Flying, Earthquake...); exclude anything that's a
// defensive, utility, buff, or proc/secondary-effect keyword unrelated to its own damage output
