      // tick, zero gap, rather than a second independently-scheduled timer landing even a few ms
      // apart: a live trace showed that even a small deliberate buffer between "Flip reverts its
      // targets" and "entrants release their pin" was enough, on its own, to reproduce the exact
      // jump this whole scheme exists to prevent — these two MUST share one clock tick, not two
      // that merely agree on paper. Only when there's no concurrent Flip.from() to hook into
