  // an in-flight setTimeout/await-sleep replay loop that closes over the match object as a
  // local `m`, but reads the module-level `matchState` singleton directly (see the many
  // `matchState.replayCards` lookups below). If the player quits/exits mid-round, endMatch()/
  // saveAndExitAsyncMatch() null out `matchState` immediately while those queued callbacks are
  // still pending — `m` stays a valid stale object, but `matchState` is null, so any of those
  // lookups threw. Nothing on-screen belongs to this event anymore once the match is torn
  // down, so just skip the VFX entirely rather than crash.
  if(!matchState) return;
