    // whichever flank half of the battlefield the attacker sat in (the 2026-09-20 fix right
    // below, kept here for history) — the intent then was "keep swinging along your own lane,"
    // but in practice an unblocked unit striking the castle reads as attacking off to one side
    // rather than straight forward at its target. A direct, unblocked castle hit now always
    // lunges straight ahead (leanX stays 0) instead of leaning toward either flank; the small
    // ±16 in-row lean below (card-vs-card, an actual neighboring target off-center) is
    // unaffected and still leans toward that real target.
    // --- superseded 2026-09-20 follow-up ("the unit on the far right attacked the Castle...
    // but it swung left when it should swing right"): a card-vs-castle hit used to lean toward
    // the HQ WIDGET's own on-screen rect — but that widget sits in the same fixed corner of its
    // row's HUD no matter which lane is attacking, so a right-flank attacker and a left-flank
    // attacker computed the exact same "lean toward the widget" direction, which happened to
    // read as "always lean left" since the widget sits at the start of the row. That version
    // instead leaned toward whichever flank half of the shared .battlefield center the attacker
